    'IT DOTH NOT YET APPEAR WHAT WE SHALL BE: HOW WE WERE MADE, WHAT WAS LOST, AND WHAT JESUS RESTORES. Yahweh made us very good: naked and not ashamed. Sin brought shame, fear and death. Samson’s strength and Elijah’s answers came from Yahweh, not from a design inside them. No son carries his father’s guilt, and Jesus prays for His own. What is coming is better than Eden: a body raised and changed at His appearing. "Beloved, now are we the sons of God, and it doth not yet appear what we shall be: but we know that, when he shall appear, we shall be like him; for we shall see him as he is." (1 John 3:2)',
